# Test Execution Plan

## 1. Introduction

This document describes the proposed process for executing and monitoring tests for the CampusConnect application. It defines the testing environment, responsibilities, test conditions, and completion criteria.

## 2. Testing Environment

The following environment is proposed for testing:

| Component | Proposed Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React.js |
| Backend | Node.js and Express.js |
| Database | MongoDB |
| API Testing | Postman |
| Unit Testing | Jest or Vitest |
| Browser Testing | Playwright |
| Version Control | Git and GitHub |

## 3. Test Data Preparation

Test data will include:

- Valid and invalid student login details.
- Sample course information.
- Assignment details and deadlines.
- Valid and invalid assignment submissions.
- Different user roles and access permissions.

Dummy data will be used instead of real student information.

## 4. Testing Responsibilities

| Role | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Developer | Write and execute unit tests |
| Tester | Prepare and execute test cases |
| Team Lead | Review testing progress and defects |
| User Representative | Provide feedback during acceptance testing |

## 5. Entry Criteria

Testing can begin when:

- Requirements are reviewed.
- The relevant module is available.
- Test cases are prepared.
- The testing environment is configured.
- Required test data is available.

## 6. Exit Criteria

A testing phase can be considered complete when:

- All planned test cases have been executed.
- Critical and high-severity defects are resolved.
- Failed test cases are reviewed and retested.
- Test results are documented.
- The team reviews the final testing report.

## 7. Test Result Documentation

Each test execution should record:

- Test case ID.
- Test date.
- Expected result.
- Actual result.
- Status (Pass or Fail).
- Defect reference, if applicable.
- Tester comments.

## 8. Conclusion

This execution plan provides a structured approach for carrying out the proposed testing activities. Following the plan will help the team monitor progress, identify defects, and evaluate the quality of CampusConnect before deployment.
